XNU Apple80211 ioctl forward, IEEE80211 media and kernel events on the Wi-Fi en0 ifnet (P-W4, T-7241; goal W-D7; research 110 s.3 and s.5).

Cause: wifid's IO80211 library talks to the interface by SIOCSA80211/SIOCGA80211 (_IOW/_IOWR 'i' 200/201, a 40-byte apple80211req whose req_data is a user
buffer), asks SIOCGIFMEDIA for IFM_IEEE80211 and reads kern_event messages (vendor 1, class 6, subclass 1, ifname[16] first). en0 (patch 0199) answered every
unknown ioctl EOPNOTSUPP and posted no Apple80211 event, so the library could neither bind nor scan.
Fix: new bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_a80211.h (the logic: copy the 40-byte request, copyin/copyout req_len bytes through req_data, call the station handler, wipe the
scratch buffer that held the ASSOCIATE body, refuse over-long and unmapped requests with a GAP line, build the kern_event post, chain every other command to
en0's own if_ioctl so SIOCGIFMEDIA keeps answering IFM_IEEE80211|IFM_AUTO), a verbatim copy of the X-W1 station handler bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_sta.h, and
bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_a80211.c (glue: copyin/copyout, one mutex, kev_post_msg_nowait, and sweet_wlan_a80211_attach() which puts the handler in front of
ifp->if_ioctl). Reachability read from XNU 22.6.0: ifioctl() (bsd/net/if.c:3184) hands an unknown 'i' command to pru_control (in_control, EOPNOTSUPP) and then
to ifnet_ioctl() -> ifp->if_ioctl, with no size check against ifreq. Generated by tools/gen-wlan-a80211-patch from shim/; shim/build.sh refuses a stale copy.
Tests: shim/wlan_a80211_glue_host_test.c (fake radio, fake user memory, fake kev_post_msg, the real en0_ioctl).
Not compiled against XNU here (CI builds the tree), not run on hardware. T-431f adds bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_radio.h (the swsta_radio backend over escan result events,
host-tested by shim/wlan_radio_host_test.c) and sweet_wlan_a80211_radio_attach(), which patch 0199's sweet_wlan_en0_init calls once en0 is up.
T-08fd wires the escan link: swr_replay_escan replays the ESCAN_RESULT events that the boot-time G2 L23 scan (patch 0174) recorded, via sweet_wlan_g2_escan_rec; no bus
access, no store; the listing is the boot-time one and says so (WIFI GAP, stale) on every scan; an empty record refuses the scan with a gap. Events carry an empty payload (WIFI GAP at attach).

